/// Shadowable prelude: loaded automatically before every Miri program, unless
/// the program declares a type of the same name.
///
/// These modules are re-exported by name like `prelude.mi`, so their types need
/// no `use`. The difference is what happens on a collision: a program that
/// declares its own `Result` keeps it, and the module here is not loaded at all.
///
/// A module belongs here only when nothing else in the stdlib depends on the
/// types it declares. Skipping a module the rest of the stdlib is written
/// against would leave that code without the type it was checked with, so those
/// modules stay in `prelude.mi`, where their names are reserved.
use system.result
